INSERT INTO "Article" ("id", "slug", "category", "country", "titleEn", "titleNe", "excerptEn", "excerptNe", "bodyEn", "bodyNe", "sources", "publishedAt", "createdAt", "updatedAt") VALUES
(gen_random_uuid(), 'ai-agent-jobs-2965-roles-november-2026-20261104', 'global', 'USA',
'AI Agent Jobs November 2026: 2,965 Open Roles, Median Pay $227,000',
'',
'AgenticCareers.co counts 2,965 open AI agent roles across 958 companies in November 2026, with a median pay of $227,000 a year among listings that disclose a range.',
'',
$$<p>AI agent jobs have reached a scale that can now be counted in the thousands, with AgenticCareers.co reporting 2,965 open agentic roles across 958 companies in its November 2026 State of Agentic Hiring report. The report, published in November 2026, puts the median pay at $227,000 a year among the 42% of listings that disclose a salary range, and says 2,054 of the roles opened in the last 30 days alone. AI Agent Engineer is the largest single category, with 481 roles, or 16.2% of the total.</p>
<table><tr><th>At a glance</th><th>Details</th></tr><tr><td>Report</td><td>State of Agentic Hiring, November 2026, AgenticCareers.co</td></tr><tr><td>Open agentic roles</td><td>2,965 across 958 companies</td></tr><tr><td>Median pay</td><td>$227,000 a year (middle half $173,000 to $285,000), across 1,239 listings that disclose pay</td></tr><tr><td>Share disclosing pay</td><td>42%</td></tr><tr><td>Roles added in the last 30 days</td><td>2,054 (69.3% of the board)</td></tr><tr><td>Largest category</td><td>AI Agent Engineer, 481 roles (16.2%)</td></tr><tr><td>Largest employer</td><td>OpenAI, 264 roles</td></tr><tr><td>Remote share</td><td>22% of listings market-wide</td></tr><tr><td>Entry-level share</td><td>110 junior and internship roles out of 2,965</td></tr><tr><td>Application route</td><td>Each employer's own careers page; the report carries no single deadline</td></tr></table>
<h2>AI agent jobs: where the roles sit</h2>
<p>AI Agent Engineer leads the board by a wide margin, with 481 roles, followed by AI Solutions Engineer with 359 roles and AI Infrastructure with 271 roles. Machine Learning Engineer accounts for 218 roles, Forward Deployed Engineer for 172, and Data Scientist for 150. AI Security follows with 148 roles, AI Researcher with 141, and LLM Engineer with 135. AI Platform and Site Reliability Engineering holds 125 roles, General AI 102, Full Stack AI 93, and Computer Vision 92. AI Safety, at 89 roles, sits below the engineering categories in count even though it carries the highest median pay in the report.</p>
<p>Growth is just as concentrated. AI Agent Engineer added 311 roles in the last 30 days, AI Solutions Engineer added 266, AI Infrastructure added 190, Machine Learning Engineer added 146, and Forward Deployed Engineer added 128. The fastest-growing work is building agents, putting them into production for customers, and running the infrastructure underneath them, rather than smaller fields such as prompt engineering, with 56 roles, or retrieval and search, with 57.</p>
<h2>AI agent jobs pay: what the disclosed ranges show</h2>
<p>Among roles with enough disclosed listings to publish a median, AI Safety pays most at $277,500 a year, closely followed by AI Researcher at $277,000. Full Stack AI sits at $269,000, AI Infrastructure at $267,925, and AI Platform and Site Reliability Engineering at $252,250. AI Security reports $247,000, Forward Deployed Engineer $230,000, and AI Sales and Go-to-Market $227,000, matching the overall median. AI Agent Engineer and AI Solutions Engineer both sit at $220,000, Data Scientist at $211,200, Machine Learning Engineer at $192,000, General AI at $185,200, and LLM Engineer at $183,750.</p>
<p>Two limits apply to every pay figure here. The report publishes a median only where at least 30 listings disclose pay, and withholds medians for smaller segments such as AI Product Manager, with 25 disclosed listings, AI Operations and DevOps, with 18, and Robotics, with 15. The median is also the midpoint of the disclosed range, in United States dollars per year, and says nothing about equity, bonuses, or location adjustments, which the report does not break out. A listing without a stated range is not evidence of low pay; it is one of the 58% of listings that do not disclose a figure.</p>
<h2>AI agent jobs: who is hiring most</h2>
<p>OpenAI leads the employer table with 264 roles, followed by Anthropic with 165, Databricks with 147, and NVIDIA with 130. Salesforce lists 69 roles, Capital One 63, Sierra 56, Harvey 51, Scale AI 49, and Adobe 42. LangChain and Cloudflare each list 39, Together AI 38, Perplexity AI 37, and JPMorganChase 36. The ten largest employers together hold 35.3% of all open roles, so a jobseeker who applies only to the best-known names is competing in just over a third of the market, while the remaining 948 companies hold the rest.</p>
<p>That spread matters for applicants who need remote work. Only 6% of listings from the ten largest employers are remote, against 22% market-wide and 41% among employers with a single open role, so smaller employers may offer better odds, even though they disclose pay less often, at 35% against 43% for the ten largest.</p>
<h2>The entry-level squeeze in AI agent jobs</h2>
<p>The seniority split is the starkest finding in the report. Mid-level roles make up 49% of the board, with 1,453 listings, followed by senior roles at 24%, with 697, staff roles at 15%, with 450, and lead roles at 8%, with 239. Internships account for 58 roles and junior roles for 52, a combined 110 entry-level listings against 450 staff-level listings, with only 16 executive roles above them. A normal engineering market, the report notes, has more junior roles than staff roles, because companies expect to grow people; this market has the shape reversed.</p>
<p>The report offers capacity, not hostility, as the likeliest explanation: agent teams are mostly small and new, assembled by moving experienced engineers across from other teams, leaving nobody whose job is to train a junior hire. It names internships as the leading indicator to watch, since junior hiring follows about a year later when internship numbers move, and notes that the entry-level roles that do exist cluster with the smallest employers. New graduates should treat an internship as the realistic entry point, and target smaller employers first.</p>
<h2>What to do next with the AI agent jobs data</h2>
<p>Start from the category, not the company name. Agent-building experience points to AI Agent Engineer and AI Solutions Engineer, where growth is fastest; infrastructure experience points to AI Infrastructure and AI Platform and Site Reliability Engineering, where medians are higher. Check each posting on the employer's own careers page before applying. There is no single deadline for this market, so each role carries its own closing date or stays open until filled.</p>
<p>Apply only through the employer's own site or a posting linked from it, and never pay to apply. No genuine employer in this report charges a fee for an application, and any message asking for payment, gift cards, or bank details in exchange for an interview should be treated as a fraud attempt. For readers weighing other paid routes into AI work, <a href="https://growentix.cloud/articles/ai-startup-jobs-13514-roles-20261104">AI startup jobs across more than 1,100 companies</a> cover permanent roles at a median base of $190,000 a year, <a href="https://growentix.cloud/articles/ai-training-jobs-software-engineers-20261104">AI training jobs for software engineers</a> pay by the hour, and the <a href="https://growentix.cloud/articles/anthropic-residency-ai-safety-20261104">Anthropic Residency</a> offers a paid fixed-term route into AI safety research.</p>
<p><small>Sources: AgenticCareers.co, "State of Agentic Hiring (November 2026)", at https://agenticcareers.co/state-of-agentic-hiring. The report states the role counts, pay medians, hiring velocity, employer table, seniority split, and remote shares quoted here; the dataset is licensed CC BY 4.0. No single application deadline applies to the listings counted in the report.</small></p>$$,
'',
ARRAY['https://agenticcareers.co/state-of-agentic-hiring'],
NOW(), NOW(), NOW())
ON CONFLICT ("slug") DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO "Article" ("id", "slug", "category", "country", "titleEn", "titleNe", "excerptEn", "excerptNe", "bodyEn", "bodyNe", "sources", "publishedAt", "createdAt", "updatedAt") VALUES
(gen_random_uuid(), 'cabinet-secretariat-dfo-technical-250-posts-20261104', 'global', 'India',
'Cabinet Secretariat DFO Recruitment 2026: 250 Technical Posts, Apply by Post by 15 November',
'',
'The Cabinet Secretariat has opened 250 Deputy Field Officer (Technical) posts for GATE-qualified Indian nationals, with applications by ordinary post reaching New Delhi by 15 November 2026.',
'',
$$<p>Cabinet Secretariat DFO recruitment 2026 offers 250 tentative posts of Deputy Field Officer (Technical) in the Government of India, and the closing date is close: applications must reach the Cabinet Secretariat by ordinary post by 15 November 2026. The notification, Advertisement No. 02/2026, was published in the Employment News issue of 17 to 23 October 2026, and it fills a Group B, non-gazetted post in Level-7 of the pay matrix, with initial monthly emoluments of about Rs. 1,00,000 including all allowances for a posting at New Delhi.</p>
<p>Read the eligibility limits first, because they narrow the field sharply. Applicants must be Indian nationals, must hold a valid GATE scorecard with qualifying cut-off marks in GATE 2024, 2025, or 2026 in the paper matching their subject, and must not be over 30 years of age as on 15 November 2026. Each applicant may apply for only one of the nine subjects, and the degree subject and GATE paper must match. There is no online form, so an applicant who waits for a portal link will miss the deadline.</p>
<table><tr><th>At a glance</th><th>Details</th></tr><tr><td>Organisation</td><td>Cabinet Secretariat, Government of India</td></tr><tr><td>Post</td><td>Deputy Field Officer (Technical)</td></tr><tr><td>Advertisement No.</td><td>02/2026</td></tr><tr><td>Total vacancies</td><td>250 (tentative, revisable at any stage)</td></tr><tr><td>Pay</td><td>Level-7, Group B, non-gazetted; about Rs. 1,00,000 a month including allowances at New Delhi</td></tr><tr><td>Notification published</td><td>Employment News, 17 to 23 October 2026 issue</td></tr><tr><td>Last date for receipt of applications</td><td>15 November 2026 (form must reach the address, not merely be posted)</td></tr><tr><td>Application mode</td><td>Offline only, by ordinary post</td></tr><tr><td>Eligibility</td><td>Indian national; B.E. or B.Tech. or M.Sc. in a notified subject; valid GATE score in the matching paper</td></tr><tr><td>Age limit</td><td>Not exceeding 30 years as on 15 November 2026; relaxation as per Central Government orders in force</td></tr><tr><td>Selection</td><td>GATE score merit list, shortlisting at five times the vacancies per subject, then interview</td></tr><tr><td>Application fee</td><td>Not mentioned in the notification</td></tr></table>
<h2>Cabinet Secretariat DFO recruitment 2026: subject-wise vacancies</h2>
<p>All 250 vacancies sit under the single post of Deputy Field Officer (Technical), split across nine subjects, and the notification marks the figures as tentative. Computer Science and Information Technology carries 112 posts, with GATE paper CS, and Electronics and Communication or Telecommunication also carries 112 posts, with GATE paper EC. Data Science and Artificial Intelligence carries 10 posts, with GATE paper DA, Physics 5 posts, with GATE paper PH, Mechanical Engineering 4, Civil Engineering 3, Chemistry 2, Mathematics 1, and Statistics 1, with GATE papers ME, CE, CY, MA, and ST respectively.</p>
<p>The notification gives no category-wise reservation split and no Persons with Benchmark Disabilities breakup, so applicants should not rely on any split figure read elsewhere. The Cabinet Secretariat may revise the number of vacancies at any stage, and may cancel or withdraw the process without giving a reason. Shortlisting is done subject by subject, so a GATE score is compared only with others in the same paper.</p>
<h2>Who can apply for the Cabinet Secretariat DFO posts</h2>
<p>Applicants need a Bachelor's degree in Engineering or Technology, or a Master's degree in Science, in one of the nine subjects, from a recognised university or institution. A valid GATE score means the applicant achieved the qualifying cut-off marks in GATE 2024, 2025, or 2026 in the paper for the subject applied for, and all eligibility conditions are counted as on 15 November 2026.</p>
<p>The maximum age is 30 years as on 15 November 2026, with relaxation for Scheduled Caste, Scheduled Tribe, Other Backward Classes, Central Government employees, and ex-servicemen as per Central Government orders in force. The notice does not state the number of relaxation years and does not mention a minimum age, so applicants claiming relaxation should check the official notification rather than assuming a figure. Persons in government service must send the form through their office with Annexure-IV if they claim age relaxation.</p>
<h2>Pay, posting, and service conditions</h2>
<p>The post sits in Level-7 of the pay matrix as a Group B, non-gazetted post, with initial monthly emoluments of about Rs. 1,00,000 including all allowances for a posting at New Delhi. The notification does not give the basic pay amount or allowance details, so those figures should not be guessed from the total. The job involves field postings with All India transfer liability, and the medical standard will follow the Central Government guidelines for Group B posts.</p>
<h2>How selection works for the Cabinet Secretariat DFO posts</h2>
<p>Selection starts with a merit list. All applications received by the closing date that meet the eligibility conditions are arranged in order of merit on valid GATE score, separately for each subject. Shortlisting is set at five times the number of vacancies in each subject, and shortlisted candidates are called for interview, with the date, time, and centre sent by email. Final selection is based on the GATE score and the interview, subject to eligibility, character and antecedent verification, and medical examination. The notification does not state the interview marks or weightage, so applicants should not assume a ratio.</p>
<h2>How to apply for the Cabinet Secretariat DFO posts by post</h2>
<p>This is an offline process with no registration portal, and the steps leave little room for error. Applicants should copy the form printed in the notification, type it on A-4 size paper in English capital letters using black or blue ink only, fill every column, affix a self-attested recent passport-size coloured photograph, and sign the declaration. Self-attested copies of Matriculation, 10+2, and degree mark sheets and certificates, proof of date of birth, the valid GATE scorecard, and the Aadhaar card must be attached, with a caste certificate in Annexure-I or II if age relaxation is claimed, and a no-objection certificate if employed. Two recent passport-size coloured photographs, with the applicant's name and date of birth on the back, are also required.</p>
<p>The completed form must be sent by ordinary post to Post Bag No. 001, Lodhi Road Head Post Office, New Delhi-110003, so that it reaches that address by 15 November 2026. The date that matters is receipt, not the date the form is dropped in a letter box, so applicants should post early and keep the postal receipt. A form that is unsigned, incomplete, or missing a photograph or certificate will not be entertained, and more than one application, or an application for more than one subject, risks rejection. No application fee or payment mode is mentioned, so applicants should not send money with the form unless the official notification asks them to.</p>
<p>For readers tracking other central openings, <a href="https://growentix.cloud/articles/gsssb-cce-1237-posts-20261104">GSSSB CCE recruitment for 1,237 posts</a> takes applications until 30 November 2026, <a href="https://growentix.cloud/articles/bob-wms-837-posts-20261104">Bank of Baroda WMS recruitment for 837 posts</a> closes on 24 November 2026, and the <a href="https://growentix.cloud/articles/supreme-court-junior-court-attendant-130-posts-20261104">Supreme Court Junior Court Attendant recruitment for 130 posts</a> closes on 25 November 2026.</p>
<p><small>Sources: GovtJobsAlert, "Cabinet Secretariat DFO (Technical) Recruitment 2026 – 250 Posts (Advt 02/2026, GATE Score), Apply Offline by 15 Nov", at https://govtjobsalert.in/cabinet-secretariat-dfo-technical-recruitment-2026/, reporting Advertisement No. 02/2026 published in Employment News, 17 to 23 October 2026; Cabinet Secretariat official website, cabsec.gov.in. The notification states the vacancy total, subject split, GATE requirement, age limit, postal address, and 15 November 2026 receipt deadline quoted here; the application fee is not mentioned in the notification, and no category-wise vacancy split is given.</small></p>$$,
'',
ARRAY['https://govtjobsalert.in/cabinet-secretariat-dfo-technical-recruitment-2026/'],
NOW(), NOW(), NOW())
ON CONFLICT ("slug") DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO "Article" ("id", "slug", "category", "country", "titleEn", "titleNe", "excerptEn", "excerptNe", "bodyEn", "bodyNe", "sources", "publishedAt", "createdAt", "updatedAt") VALUES
(gen_random_uuid(), 'rites-apprentice-281-posts-20261104', 'global', 'India',
'RITES Apprentice Recruitment 2026: 281 Posts, Apply 5 to 25 November',
'',
'RITES Limited has opened 281 apprentice seats for 2026-27, with online applications from 5 November 2026 to 25 November 2026 and selection on academic merit only.',
'',
$$<p>RITES apprentice recruitment 2026 has opened 281 apprentice seats for the 2026-27 training year, with online applications running from 5 November 2026 to 25 November 2026. RITES Limited, a Navratna Central Public Sector Enterprise under the Ministry of Railways, issued the notice as Advertisement No. Pers./26-10/Apprentice/2026-27/01, dated 4 November 2026, for a one-year programme for degree, diploma, and ITI pass-outs. The notice itself states the total as 281, and its category figures add up to the same total, which settles a conflicting headline elsewhere that put the figure at 286.</p>
<p>Read the two-step application rule first, because registering on a portal alone does not complete the application. Candidates must first register and apply on the National Apprenticeship Training Scheme portal, for degree and diploma holders, or the National Apprenticeship Promotion Scheme portal, for ITI pass-outs, then submit scanned documents through the separate RITES form by 25 November 2026. Documents submitted by email or hard copy will not be considered.</p>
<table><tr><th>At a glance</th><th>Details</th></tr><tr><td>Organisation</td><td>RITES Limited, a Navratna Central Public Sector Enterprise under the Ministry of Railways</td></tr><tr><td>Programme</td><td>Apprenticeship Training Programme, FY 2026-27, one year, not extendable</td></tr><tr><td>Advertisement No.</td><td>Pers./26-10/Apprentice/2026-27/01, dated 4 November 2026</td></tr><tr><td>Total seats</td><td>281</td></tr><tr><td>Application window</td><td>5 November 2026 to 25 November 2026 on the NATS or NAPS portal, with documents through the RITES form by 25 November 2026</td></tr><tr><td>Stipend</td><td>Rs. 15,650 a month for Graduate Apprentices, Rs. 13,450 for Diploma Apprentices, Rs. 10,560 for Trade Apprentices</td></tr><tr><td>Selection</td><td>Merit list on percentage of marks in the essential qualification; no written test and no interview</td></tr><tr><td>Minimum marks</td><td>60% in aggregate for General and EWS, 50% for SC, ST, OBC (NCL), and PwBD against reserved positions</td></tr><tr><td>Age condition</td><td>Must have completed 18 years as on 5 November 2026</td></tr><tr><td>Posting</td><td>Across India; location preference is considered but final posting rests with RITES</td></tr></table>
<h2>RITES apprentice recruitment 2026: seats and stipend by category</h2>
<p>Graduate Apprentice (Engineering) carries 125 seats for four-year full-time BE, B.Tech., or B.Arch. degrees, at Rs. 15,650 a month including a direct benefit transfer of Rs. 6,150. Graduate Apprentice (Non-Engineering) carries 43 seats for three-year BA, BBA, B.Com., B.Sc., or BCA degrees, at the same stipend. Diploma Apprentice carries 62 seats for three-year full-time engineering diplomas, at Rs. 13,450 a month including a direct benefit transfer of Rs. 5,450. Trade Apprentice carries 51 seats for full-time ITI pass-outs, at Rs. 10,560 a month. Those four figures add up to 281.</p>
<p>The category-wise split gives 32 Scheduled Caste seats, 12 Scheduled Tribe seats, 68 Other Backward Classes seats, 21 Economically Weaker Section seats, and 144 unreserved seats, with 4 Persons with Benchmark Disabilities seats on a horizontal basis. Within Graduate (Engineering), Civil carries 40 seats and Mechanical 36; Graduate (Non-Engineering) splits into Finance 21 and Human Resources 22; and ITI trades split into Mechanical 23 and Electrical 23. Persons with Benchmark Disabilities candidates must hold a certificate for a disability of not less than 40%.</p>
<h2>Who can apply for the RITES apprentice seats</h2>
<p>The essential qualification for each trade must come from a recognised university or institute, recognised by the University Grants Commission or the All India Council for Technical Education for degree and diploma qualifications, or by the National Council or State Council for Vocational Training for ITI qualifications. Shortlisting is by a merit list on the percentage of marks in the essential qualification, with no written test or interview. Where the qualification specifies marks in an honours subject, those marks are considered; otherwise the aggregate of all subjects is considered. If two applicants have the same marks, the older applicant is placed higher.</p>
<p>The minimum qualifying marks are 60% in aggregate for General and Economically Weaker Section candidates, and 50% for Scheduled Caste, Scheduled Tribe, Other Backward Classes (non-creamy layer), and Persons with Benchmark Disabilities candidates against reserved positions. A candidate may apply for only one post, and if more than one application is submitted, only the latest valid completed application will be considered. A location preference may be indicated in the RITES form, although the final posting is decided on the requirements of RITES.</p>
<h2>Who cannot apply for the RITES apprentice seats</h2>
<p>The notice lists five exclusions, all counted as on 5 November 2026. Candidates awaiting the result of the essential qualification on that date cannot apply, nor can candidates who have not completed 18 years of age on that date, candidates who have already undergone or are pursuing apprenticeship training under the Apprentices Act, 1961, candidates with training or job experience of one year or more after attaining the essential qualification, or degree and diploma candidates whose final semester result date falls before 5 November 2021. For ITI candidates there is no restriction on the year of attainment.</p>
<h2>How to apply for the RITES apprentice seats</h2>
<p>The application has two parts, both due by 25 November 2026. First, degree and diploma candidates must register with a complete profile on the National Apprenticeship Training Scheme portal and apply with RITES Limited as the establishment name, while ITI candidates do the same on the National Apprenticeship Promotion Scheme portal. Applicants must check that all profile details appear correctly, and contact the NATS or NAPS office for any correction.</p>
<p>Second, after applying on the portal, candidates must fill the RITES application form and submit scanned documents by 25 November 2026 through apprentice.rites.com/ApprenticeForm. The documents are the essential qualification certificates, meaning mark sheets for all semesters or years and the final passing certificate, with a conversion formula where a CGPA system applies; date-of-birth proof; identity proof; and a caste or category certificate where applicable. Other Backward Classes (non-creamy layer) certificates must be in the central format and issued on or after 5 November 2025. All documents must be clubbed into a single PDF of at most 10 MB, submitted once only, through the RITES form only.</p>
<h2>Selection, joining, and what this apprenticeship is not</h2>
<p>After receipt of applications and verification of documents, RITES will prepare a merit list on the criteria in the notice. Shortlisted candidates will be informed by email from apprenticeship@rites.com to join within a stipulated time, and the list will also be uploaded on the RITES website. Original documents are verified at joining only. Unfilled vacancies will be considered from subsequent merit lists.</p>
<p>Applicants should be clear about what the programme does not offer. RITES states that it has no obligation to offer employment during or after the apprenticeship, the training lasts only one year and will not be extended, and mere selection in empanelment confers no right of engagement. Queries go only by email to apprenticeship@rites.com, with the registration number, full name, and contact details. For readers tracking other apprenticeship openings, <a href="https://growentix.cloud/articles/nicl-graduate-apprentice-200-posts-20261104">NICL Graduate Apprentice recruitment for 200 seats</a> closes on 18 November 2026, <a href="https://growentix.cloud/articles/indian-bank-apprentice-1500-posts-20261104">Indian Bank Apprentice recruitment for 1,500 seats</a> closes on 25 November 2026, and the <a href="https://growentix.cloud/articles/rrc-central-railway-act-apprentice-2861-posts-20261104">RRC Central Railway Act Apprentice recruitment for 2,861 seats</a> is also open.</p>
<p><small>Sources: RITES Limited, Advertisement No. Pers./26-10/Apprentice/2026-27/01, "Engagement of Apprentices" for FY 2026-27, dated 4 November 2026, at https://rites.com/Upload/Career/Advertisment_for_Engagement_of_Apprentices_for_FY_2026_27_(2)_pdf-2026-Nov-04-16-7-17.pdf; Northeast Now, "Assam Career 2026: RITES Recruitment [286 posts]", published 4 November 2026, at https://m.nenow.in/article/assam-career/assam-career-2026-rites-recruitment-286-posts/546772/amp. The official notice states the total as 281, and its category figures sum to 281; the Northeast Now headline figure of 286 does not match its own category breakdown.</small></p>$$,
'',
ARRAY['https://rites.com/Upload/Career/Advertisment_for_Engagement_of_Apprentices_for_FY_2026_27_(2)_pdf-2026-Nov-04-16-7-17.pdf','https://m.nenow.in/article/assam-career/assam-career-2026-rites-recruitment-286-posts/546772/amp'],
NOW(), NOW(), NOW())
ON CONFLICT ("slug") DO NOTHING;
